                <pb facs="0446" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6315: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-24T13:00:00+08:00">May 24, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 24—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>482. Mr. S. G. Cheng, confidential aide to Huang Fu, called this morning and
                    informed me that a preliminary arrangement had been arrived at between Japanese
                    and Chinese military for a cessation of hostilities beginning last night; that
                    this was to be followed by discussions between delegates duly appointed by the
                    Japanese and Chinese military for final arrangements.</p>
                <p>Repeated Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
